WEBVTT

00:07.583 --> 00:12.375
The Kyohachi-ryu School was
the birthplace of swordsmanship.

00:12.458 --> 00:15.958
Many believe its legend ended long ago.

00:17.625 --> 00:20.500
But the eight successors
lived on in silence

00:20.583 --> 00:23.875
and immersed themselves
in ceaseless training.

00:38.000 --> 00:39.500
I'll beat you this time!

00:50.333 --> 00:51.625
Ow! That hurt!

00:55.291 --> 00:57.916
What's wrong, Iroha?
Is that the best you can do?

00:58.416 --> 00:59.791
Shut up, Sansuke!

01:27.583 --> 01:29.500
All right, you win, Shikura.

01:29.583 --> 01:31.041
If you hadn't held back, I wouldn't.

01:31.125 --> 01:32.833
I know you better than that.

01:41.583 --> 01:43.375
-Guess I'll have a bit more.
-Mmm.

01:43.458 --> 01:44.875
Going for another bowl, Jinroku?

01:44.958 --> 01:47.458
-He's insatiable.
-Ten bowls by now? Is that right?

01:47.541 --> 01:49.291
-Amazing.
-Yeah.

01:49.375 --> 01:50.208
Have you heard?

01:50.291 --> 01:52.250
Satsuma and Choshu are allies now, right?

01:52.333 --> 01:53.166
-They are.
-Right.

01:53.250 --> 01:55.333
The rebels versus the shogunate.
I wonder who'll win.

01:55.416 --> 01:58.833
Whoever knows how to use us effectively,
of course. Right, Shu-nii?

01:58.916 --> 02:00.583
Yeah, that's right.

02:00.666 --> 02:04.125
-Are we gonna join the war too?
-Master's the one who decides that.

02:04.208 --> 02:07.333
After training for all these years,
I'm looking forward to a real fight.

02:07.416 --> 02:10.250
-I know.
-Any side Sansuke joins is bound to lose.

02:10.333 --> 02:12.041
Huh?

02:12.125 --> 02:14.291
You keep crying every time
I destroy you in training.

02:14.375 --> 02:15.625
-Did you forget?
-Who? Me?

02:16.208 --> 02:17.791
-Every single time.
-You're one to talk!

02:17.875 --> 02:20.875
-All I remember is you tripping!
-Can we not do this right now?

02:30.250 --> 02:31.833
We'll do it tomorrow.

02:32.625 --> 02:34.750
There is no time left for me.

02:37.458 --> 02:38.708
It's settled.

02:50.250 --> 02:51.333
Oh!

03:10.916 --> 03:14.166
I have something to say. Listen closely.

03:15.458 --> 03:16.541
For ten years,

03:17.166 --> 03:21.291
you've endured the hardships
of rigorous training together as one.

03:23.375 --> 03:24.583
Today,

03:26.208 --> 03:28.416
that chapter comes to an end.

03:32.875 --> 03:35.125
The Kyohachi-ryu School

03:35.833 --> 03:37.666
has only one heir.

03:40.166 --> 03:42.625
The seat of succession remains unfilled.

03:42.708 --> 03:44.625
You are to fight each other for it.

03:47.666 --> 03:48.916
To the death.

03:52.291 --> 03:56.333
Tomorrow, once the sun reaches its peak,
you will begin fighting.

03:56.416 --> 03:57.375
From this moment on,

03:57.458 --> 04:00.166
forget that you ever
considered yourselves family.

04:01.250 --> 04:03.583
No one is allowed to run.

04:19.708 --> 04:21.083
This is our fate.

04:23.166 --> 04:25.291
We all knew it would come to this.

04:25.875 --> 04:26.791
Hey.

04:27.791 --> 04:29.875
Why don't we flee somewhere secluded?

04:29.958 --> 04:33.000
We could escape this mountain
and find shelter where he can't follow us.

04:33.083 --> 04:35.000
-As long as we're together--
-No.

04:35.083 --> 04:36.416
Gentosai will find us.

04:36.500 --> 04:38.583
Gentosai is nothing but an empty threat!

04:38.666 --> 04:40.625
No, he's real.

04:40.708 --> 04:42.041
He's out there.

04:42.750 --> 04:44.833
There was a time
I saw him speaking with Master.

04:46.625 --> 04:48.250
And that was no man.

04:48.833 --> 04:49.958
That was a monster.

04:51.875 --> 04:54.375
We've walked the path
of Kyohachi-ryu for a long time.

04:55.041 --> 04:56.791
We always knew this day would come.

04:57.625 --> 04:58.708
It's no use.

04:59.916 --> 05:02.083
This is our burden to bear.

05:02.750 --> 05:03.791
Right.

05:08.166 --> 05:09.083
We have no choice.

05:30.375 --> 05:31.375
Shu-nii…

05:36.041 --> 05:37.750
What are we supposed to do?

07:15.958 --> 07:18.083
How many of our men have fallen? Hm?

07:18.166 --> 07:19.208
A total of 15.

07:20.833 --> 07:23.750
Kokushu the Manslayer. He's insane!

07:24.791 --> 07:26.125
What are the boss's thoughts?

07:26.208 --> 07:29.875
As you may know, the rules do not
explicitly forbid killing our own team,

07:29.958 --> 07:31.500
and so we will be resuming the game.

07:31.583 --> 07:34.333
Oh. That's something.

07:34.416 --> 07:37.583
We have already informed Saga Shujiro
about this as well.

07:40.583 --> 07:43.708
A total of 192 participants
have been eliminated.

07:43.791 --> 07:46.541
In fact, the first participant
to leave Tenryuji Temple,

07:46.625 --> 07:49.041
number 19,
Kikuomi Ukyo, has been eliminated.

07:49.125 --> 07:50.375
Oh no!

07:50.458 --> 07:53.708
Reportedly, he lost
in a one-on-one duel with Kanjiya Bukotsu.

07:53.791 --> 07:56.666
Oh. Bukotsu the Savage Slasher.

07:56.750 --> 07:59.416
He's shaping up
to be another promising bet.

08:02.291 --> 08:05.875
Gentlemen, if you're ready now,
may we begin right away?

08:07.541 --> 08:10.791
Of course! It's what brought us here
in the first place, isn't it?

08:13.166 --> 08:17.375
Now, allow me to explain
how the wager works once again.

08:17.458 --> 08:19.583
You are betting on several
stages of the game.

08:19.666 --> 08:23.666
You are to choose which participant will
reach the next station before the rest.

08:23.750 --> 08:26.791
The first wager is
on who'll reach Seki first

08:26.875 --> 08:29.208
after crossing the Suzuka Pass.

08:29.291 --> 08:31.541
Go ahead, make your selections.

08:34.000 --> 08:36.541
Number 66, Kanjiya Bukotsu.

08:36.625 --> 08:38.500
The Suzuka Pass has many challenges.

08:38.583 --> 08:41.833
It'll take a truly strong warrior
to be able to get through that checkpoint.

08:41.916 --> 08:44.916
Two hundred, Yoshida Naoto.
Two hundred and one, Yoshida Shoji.

08:45.541 --> 08:46.750
Oh!

08:46.833 --> 08:48.916
The spear twins, interesting.

08:49.000 --> 08:51.041
So you have a fondness
for the unconventional.

08:51.125 --> 08:53.583
At Tenryuji,
they demonstrated exceptional skill.

08:53.666 --> 08:56.583
-A solid bet, I'd say.
-Mmm.

08:56.666 --> 08:58.458
Thirty-three, Tsuge Kyojin.

08:58.541 --> 08:59.458
Oh.

09:00.000 --> 09:00.875
As for me,

09:00.958 --> 09:03.333
108, Saga Shujiro.

09:03.958 --> 09:07.083
Gentlemen, you have placed your bets.

09:07.166 --> 09:10.708
So, without further delay,
let us proceed with the first round.

09:10.791 --> 09:13.166
-Please enjoy to your heart's content.
-Great.

09:21.583 --> 09:25.291
SUZUKA PASS, MIE

09:43.041 --> 09:45.333
This is the beginning
of the mountain pass.

09:45.416 --> 09:48.291
The only way
to Seki is going to be through here.

09:48.375 --> 09:50.416
We'll surely run into contestants soon.

09:50.500 --> 09:51.791
Stay close.

09:53.375 --> 09:54.375
Yes, sir.

09:59.875 --> 10:00.958
What's wrong?

10:07.083 --> 10:09.083
You said all you knew was how to kill.

10:09.166 --> 10:10.958
And they call you Manslayer.

10:13.916 --> 10:17.625
So I was wondering,
what in your life has led you to that?

10:20.750 --> 10:21.750
Well…

10:23.625 --> 10:26.000
I grew up in the mountains
with my siblings at my side.

10:26.083 --> 10:28.208
Your siblings?

10:28.875 --> 10:31.208
We were all orphans taken in by Master.

10:32.083 --> 10:33.125
We shared no blood ties.

10:34.500 --> 10:35.791
Out there,

10:37.291 --> 10:40.666
all we did was train
in order to master the skill of slaying.

10:45.291 --> 10:47.583
And did you live there your whole life?

10:47.666 --> 10:52.416
No. I took countless lives in Kyoto,
working for the Satsuma clan.

10:54.125 --> 10:56.500
Then the war came,
and I carried on killing.

10:57.083 --> 10:58.791
And before I knew it,

11:00.583 --> 11:03.208
they were calling me
Kokushu the Manslayer.

11:41.708 --> 11:42.916
Ready your sword.

11:57.083 --> 11:58.583
So you survived Tenryuji Temple?

12:00.208 --> 12:03.250
Are you still too scared
to draw your sword?

12:32.625 --> 12:33.875
Naoto!

12:35.125 --> 12:37.708
Futaba, run!

12:52.583 --> 12:55.000
Futaba!

13:02.166 --> 13:03.750
-Are you all right?
-Yes.

13:05.458 --> 13:06.708
Go.

13:17.458 --> 13:18.625
What is this?

13:26.541 --> 13:27.916
Someone's nearby.

13:40.166 --> 13:43.000
I've waited a long time for this,
Saga Shujiro!

13:43.083 --> 13:44.458
Iroha!

13:44.541 --> 13:46.750
Stop!
I don't want to fight my little sister!

13:46.833 --> 13:48.875
I'll hear none of it!

13:48.958 --> 13:50.291
Do you have any idea

13:50.375 --> 13:52.541
what we have all suffered through
because of you?

13:55.166 --> 13:58.166
Have you ever spared a thought
for the siblings you cast aside?

13:58.791 --> 14:00.250
You have no idea what it was like

14:00.333 --> 14:03.875
for us to leave the mountain
and live as though we were mere ghosts.

14:06.833 --> 14:08.166
I'm sorry.

14:49.333 --> 14:51.166
Retreat! Retreat! Iroha!

14:52.208 --> 14:53.416
Come.

14:59.833 --> 15:01.500
Iroha, to the front!

15:45.625 --> 15:49.125
I can't protect you at every moment.
Defend yourself or perish.

16:12.041 --> 16:13.375
Move in!

16:17.500 --> 16:18.958
Surround them! Push forward!

16:19.583 --> 16:21.250
Move up! Go!

16:22.916 --> 16:24.333
No! Get back here!

16:26.666 --> 16:28.458
You fool! What are you doing?

16:28.541 --> 16:29.916
Stay back! Keep your distance!

16:32.625 --> 16:34.958
Aim for the brat! Get her! The brat!

16:52.208 --> 16:54.416
Get the woman and the girl!

17:21.791 --> 17:23.291
Who the hell is that?

17:28.208 --> 17:29.500
He's gonna kill me!

17:44.958 --> 17:46.291
Sheathe your swords.

17:48.583 --> 17:50.583
Why did you lend your aid?

17:52.500 --> 17:54.166
It's the old way of our kin.

17:56.333 --> 17:58.041
Shedding the blood
of a child is considered

17:58.125 --> 18:00.208
to be among the greatest of evils.

18:00.708 --> 18:03.500
Those who shield the children
earn our respect.

18:04.083 --> 18:05.666
Thus, I will not engage.

18:05.750 --> 18:07.583
You think we'd take your word so easily?

18:18.666 --> 18:20.083
Oh. Uh, wait!

18:24.333 --> 18:25.875
Thank you so much, sir.

18:28.000 --> 18:30.000
Could you tell me your name, please?

18:31.416 --> 18:32.500
Kamuykocha.

18:36.916 --> 18:39.541
So long as the child is with you,
my arrows won't strike.

18:43.750 --> 18:45.625
Kamuykocha. Huh.

18:46.291 --> 18:47.958
-He's Ainu.
-Ainu?

18:48.041 --> 18:50.125
The indigenous people of the north.

18:50.208 --> 18:52.666
I saw them during the Battle of Hakodate.

18:52.750 --> 18:56.458
I suppose the rumors were true.
The newspapers made it up to Hokkaido.

18:59.333 --> 19:00.500
95, 106

19:00.583 --> 19:02.083
We can pass through Seki with this.

19:03.750 --> 19:05.750
More participants are
surely coming this way.

19:05.833 --> 19:07.541
We need to keep moving.

19:10.375 --> 19:11.458
Iroha.

19:12.250 --> 19:13.375
Take this.

19:20.208 --> 19:22.125
If you truly mean to kill me,

19:23.333 --> 19:25.375
you'll have to reach Tokyo first.

19:36.583 --> 19:37.416
Wait.

19:42.375 --> 19:43.916
Fine, I'll come with you.

19:50.583 --> 19:53.041
There's still something left
you must see through.

19:55.500 --> 19:57.666
You can't run off anymore.

20:04.875 --> 20:05.958
All right.

20:21.125 --> 20:24.166
-Are you sure that's enough?
-Carrying too many puts us at risk.

20:24.250 --> 20:25.333
Let's move.

20:45.958 --> 20:46.875
Come in.

20:50.375 --> 20:51.666
If you'll excuse me.

20:52.208 --> 20:54.083
I'm here with an update
on the investigation.

20:54.166 --> 20:55.208
Mm-hmm.

20:55.291 --> 20:59.708
Kyoto authorities have found blood
and scattered human remains, sir.

20:59.791 --> 21:02.666
They've received countless testimonies
of sword fights taking place

21:02.750 --> 21:05.666
between individuals
believed to be shizoku.

21:06.750 --> 21:10.791
Furthermore, the eyewitness reports
aren't only from a single village.

21:10.875 --> 21:14.458
Shiga, Mie, they're moving as well.

21:14.541 --> 21:17.250
Are you saying the shizoku
are killing each other as they travel?

21:17.333 --> 21:18.666
Indeed.

21:19.250 --> 21:20.291
Also,

21:21.333 --> 21:24.250
it looks like their course leads
from Kyoto toward Tokyo.

21:25.125 --> 21:26.583
Or so it would seem.

21:27.125 --> 21:29.041
So they're moving towards us?

21:29.125 --> 21:30.833
It doesn't stop there, sir.

21:30.916 --> 21:34.458
There were also countless reports
of gunshots at Tenryuji Temple.

21:36.458 --> 21:37.666
Lord Okubo,

21:37.750 --> 21:40.958
a large group of shizoku
wielding swords and bayonets are advancing

21:41.041 --> 21:44.625
toward the capital, which means
that this is a planned insurrection

21:44.708 --> 21:47.458
started by shizoku discontented
with the current government regime--

21:47.541 --> 21:51.166
If they were planning a rebellion,
they wouldn't be killing each other.

21:51.250 --> 21:52.125
Yes. But sir…

21:56.375 --> 21:58.291
Hm. I understand.

21:59.208 --> 22:02.375
If ignored,
it may escalate into a national crisis.

22:02.458 --> 22:06.083
Kawaji, track down the source
of the guns right away.

22:06.166 --> 22:09.541
Maejima, comb through
the past month's telegraph records.

22:09.625 --> 22:11.458
There may be something,
traces they left behind.

22:11.541 --> 22:12.375
Yes, sir.

22:26.250 --> 22:28.041
TENRYUJI TEMPLE

22:34.125 --> 22:37.166
SEKI

22:46.666 --> 22:49.083
SEKI-JUKU

22:49.166 --> 22:52.125
REQUIRED POINTS: 3

23:03.833 --> 23:05.958
We're nearly at the exit, right?

23:06.041 --> 23:08.791
There should be someone
here to check our tags.

23:36.333 --> 23:38.166
No need to be so wary.

23:39.500 --> 23:43.083
Pleased to make your acquaintance,
I'll be the one in charge of your passage.

23:43.166 --> 23:45.125
My name is Tsurubami.

23:48.333 --> 23:50.083
Your wooden tags, please.

23:59.625 --> 24:00.875
Saga Shujiro,

24:00.958 --> 24:02.166
three tags.

24:02.916 --> 24:04.458
Katsuki Futaba, three tags.

24:05.041 --> 24:07.041
Kinugasa Iroha, five tags.

24:08.875 --> 24:11.333
Points confirmed.
You are all free to pass.

24:13.000 --> 24:14.375
This is for you, Miss Kinugasa.

24:18.541 --> 24:20.416
This red tag counts for three points.

24:20.500 --> 24:24.250
You will take it in place of three tags
that are not marked with your number.

24:25.958 --> 24:27.083
Tsurubami, was it?

24:29.041 --> 24:31.750
-Yes.
-What exactly is your purpose with this?

24:31.833 --> 24:34.625
-I can't answer that, I'm afraid.
-Then I'll ask something else.

24:36.250 --> 24:40.000
-Who made this whole thing up anyway?
-I can't answer that either.

24:40.083 --> 24:41.041
However…

24:43.500 --> 24:45.958
truthfully,
I am quite certain the both of you

24:46.916 --> 24:49.250
have experienced Kodoku once already.

24:51.541 --> 24:52.833
What are you implying?

24:55.333 --> 24:56.791
Three bugs, right?

25:05.000 --> 25:08.125
Well then, have a safe journey.

25:25.416 --> 25:26.416
Mmm.

25:32.166 --> 25:33.625
Gentlemen,

25:34.958 --> 25:38.166
we have received news that all contestants
have reached the checkpoint now.

25:38.250 --> 25:40.250
Mm. Who won?

25:40.333 --> 25:42.583
The first participant
to pass through Seki…

25:42.666 --> 25:43.833
Hm?

25:44.583 --> 25:47.500
-…was number 33, Tsuge Kyojin.
-Oh yes!

25:49.833 --> 25:51.041
Well, well.

25:51.125 --> 25:52.958
Looks like I've won this round, gentlemen.

25:53.041 --> 25:58.250
Argh, you dog! Hm. I'll be damned!

25:58.333 --> 26:00.750
As expected of a former ninja from Iga.

26:00.833 --> 26:03.166
Well, Mr. Morosawa,
that's unfortunate for us.

26:03.250 --> 26:06.750
-Maybe we were too ambitious, right?
-It's only the first round.

26:06.833 --> 26:09.916
-We've got plenty of chances to recover.
-Yes, naturally.

26:10.000 --> 26:12.916
And then there's number 277, Kamuykocha.

26:13.000 --> 26:15.458
Never thought
I'd see an Ainu take part in this.

26:15.541 --> 26:18.875
Yes, well, this is quite unpredictable,
wouldn't you say so?

26:18.958 --> 26:22.625
It appears the organizer's really
outdone himself with this game, right?

26:22.708 --> 26:26.416
I cannot thank him enough for this.

26:27.208 --> 26:31.083
Now, if you're ready,
let us proceed with the second bet.

26:31.875 --> 26:36.000
Our second wager is on who shall arrive
first at the next checkpoint in Chiryu.

26:43.250 --> 26:47.666
YOKKAICHI-JUKU

26:59.000 --> 27:00.458
I take it you're Mr. Saga?

27:01.500 --> 27:03.416
We've been expecting you.

27:03.500 --> 27:05.250
Welcome. Please, come in.

27:20.958 --> 27:22.458
I knew you would come.

27:23.041 --> 27:27.083
You have a keen sense of survival.
You're a seasoned warrior after all.

27:27.583 --> 27:29.250
Why did you choose Yokkaichi?

27:29.333 --> 27:31.416
I thought you realized I'm a strategist.

27:31.500 --> 27:35.500
The Suzuka Pass isn't easy.
And taking it with a girl who can't fight?

27:35.583 --> 27:37.583
You had your hands full.

27:38.291 --> 27:41.958
I'm sure you thought many times
of forming our alliance after that.

27:45.125 --> 27:47.916
Turns out
you wanted more than just one alliance.

27:48.541 --> 27:50.333
You found yourself
a fair lady to bring along.

27:50.416 --> 27:52.125
-Shut your mouth.
-No, ma'am, I won't.

27:52.208 --> 27:53.916
Hello, how are you?

27:54.416 --> 27:57.416
Kyojin's the name.
And you're Kinugasa Iroha.

27:58.041 --> 27:59.541
How do you know my name?

28:00.583 --> 28:02.875
I'm a strategist, I already told you.

28:06.208 --> 28:07.333
Kyojin.

28:10.500 --> 28:13.000
I cannot say I trust you just yet,

28:13.833 --> 28:14.833
but…

28:16.333 --> 28:19.083
I do want to increase
my chances of survival.

28:21.791 --> 28:24.125
You know what Kodoku means too, right?

28:27.000 --> 28:28.625
Three bugs, is that it?

28:29.333 --> 28:30.166
Yes.

28:34.083 --> 28:36.083
This is how you write

28:36.833 --> 28:38.125
Kodoku.

28:41.875 --> 28:45.333
Hundreds of insects trapped in a jar,
forced to fight to the death.

28:46.250 --> 28:49.500
The last insect to survive
then becomes a god

28:49.583 --> 28:52.375
and becomes strong enough
to conquer everything.

28:53.333 --> 28:55.666
You seem well versed in that.

28:57.500 --> 28:59.750
Iroha and I have been
through this already.

29:01.041 --> 29:03.041
We were once like bugs in a jar.

29:15.166 --> 29:17.541
Quite the life, huh?

29:17.625 --> 29:19.750
So this is your second Kodoku then?
Oh dear.

29:23.375 --> 29:25.791
Well, back to what you were saying.

29:26.333 --> 29:28.166
If that's the true meaning of Kodoku,

29:28.250 --> 29:32.208
then it's safe to assume
there can only be one survivor in the end.

29:34.166 --> 29:35.208
So, Saga,

29:35.916 --> 29:38.000
do you consider yourself prepared?

29:39.750 --> 29:41.791
Will you kill everyone at your side?

29:46.125 --> 29:48.833
There is someone I must save
before it's too late.

29:50.750 --> 29:51.791
Still…

29:53.291 --> 29:56.125
I won't be playing this Kodoku
the way they want to play.

30:03.458 --> 30:06.791
Oh my. Looks like seeking you out
was a great call after all.

30:09.375 --> 30:13.375
We're forming our new alliance then,
Saga Kokushu.

30:18.125 --> 30:19.500
What are you doing?

30:19.583 --> 30:23.125
They call it a handshake,
where you just grab one another's hands.

30:23.208 --> 30:25.583
This is how
people greet one another abroad.

30:25.666 --> 30:28.666
It means, "I hold nothing
in my hands and I trust you."

30:40.833 --> 30:41.833
You too, little miss.

30:45.791 --> 30:46.916
Katsuki Futaba, sir.

30:47.000 --> 30:48.416
It's an honor.

30:49.291 --> 30:50.250
Uh…

30:50.333 --> 30:51.333
What is it?

30:52.000 --> 30:55.875
I'm just really confused.
What is their purpose with this?

30:57.000 --> 30:58.958
Why force us to kill each other?

31:00.083 --> 31:02.208
Why offer 100,000 yen as the prize?

31:03.875 --> 31:06.208
Exactly. That's the real problem here.

31:06.791 --> 31:09.125
We have to understand their purpose.

31:09.208 --> 31:12.500
Otherwise, we might end up playing
right into their hands.

31:13.166 --> 31:15.291
I guess that means
we should come up with a plan then.

31:15.958 --> 31:17.833
As a matter of fact, I have a plan.

31:17.916 --> 31:19.541
That's the reason I came here to you.

31:19.625 --> 31:21.958
What exactly are you plotting?

31:24.583 --> 31:27.625
We're going to discover
all the secrets behind this Kodoku.

31:28.291 --> 31:31.208
And to accomplish that,
we'll need to conduct some tests.

31:31.291 --> 31:32.791
What sort of tests?

31:36.875 --> 31:39.291
Well, I'll give you
all the details tomorrow.

31:39.375 --> 31:41.000
Something to look forward to.

31:41.958 --> 31:43.916
Make sure you rest up, all right?

31:51.791 --> 31:55.833
KODOKU

31:55.916 --> 31:57.333
To the death.

32:44.583 --> 32:45.791
Shu-nii.

32:48.625 --> 32:49.791
Where are you going?

32:51.916 --> 32:53.166
Outhouse.

33:34.500 --> 33:35.500
What is that?

33:38.125 --> 33:39.500
Gentosai?

34:44.958 --> 34:46.916
Why are you traveling with that child?

34:50.541 --> 34:54.208
We met at Tenryuji Temple
and have stuck together since.

34:54.291 --> 34:55.458
That's all.

34:56.666 --> 34:59.041
You don't really believe
she'll survive, do you?

35:06.708 --> 35:08.750
Is this your way
of trying to find atonement

35:10.625 --> 35:12.791
after abandoning us on that mountain?

35:33.291 --> 35:34.458
Iroha,

35:36.375 --> 35:38.500
I'd like to hear what happened after that.

35:39.416 --> 35:40.916
If you're willing to share.

35:48.583 --> 35:50.000
Master was afraid.

35:51.458 --> 35:54.708
He didn't want the school's secrets
falling into outside hands.

35:55.541 --> 35:57.625
That's why he wanted us all to die.

36:01.416 --> 36:03.291
Ikkan stood up to him.

36:04.750 --> 36:06.416
He turned his sword on Master.

36:06.500 --> 36:08.500
We all owe our escape to that.

36:11.625 --> 36:14.750
We were fortunate enough
to find our way off the mountain.

36:16.791 --> 36:18.416
After that, we were scattered.

36:22.625 --> 36:25.583
I wasn't even allowed
to wield a sword as a woman.

36:31.666 --> 36:33.333
Gentosai didn't care.

36:35.208 --> 36:37.416
He haunted every shadow I saw.

36:42.166 --> 36:43.791
And it all began

36:45.250 --> 36:47.708
on the day that you decided to run.

36:59.125 --> 37:00.791
I'm very sorry.

37:16.333 --> 37:18.416
Why did you decide to join this game?

37:21.416 --> 37:23.500
My daughter died from cholera.

37:25.666 --> 37:27.208
My wife is dying.

37:28.750 --> 37:31.000
My son may catch it as well.

37:32.291 --> 37:34.166
And I don't have the money
to buy medicine.

37:34.250 --> 37:35.541
Is that so?

37:37.958 --> 37:40.250
Never thought I'd see you as a father.

37:43.583 --> 37:44.458
And yourself?

37:46.291 --> 37:48.250
Why did you join this Kodoku?

37:50.750 --> 37:53.208
You said there was something
I must see through.

37:58.708 --> 38:01.166
I don't know
if you should be involved in it.

38:03.750 --> 38:05.625
I will decide soon enough.

38:19.166 --> 38:20.375
Iroha.

38:26.166 --> 38:28.125
I admit to running away then.

38:32.000 --> 38:33.458
And I understand

38:35.125 --> 38:37.958
I have made you suffer deeply
because of that.

38:39.541 --> 38:41.375
And you can hate me for it.

38:43.041 --> 38:44.458
Still,

38:45.708 --> 38:48.125
seeing you breathing and standing strong…

38:52.958 --> 38:55.041
means the world to me.

39:18.916 --> 39:21.333
We need two more tags
to pass through Chiryu.

39:21.833 --> 39:24.791
We should collect them
while there's still a crowd.

39:24.875 --> 39:26.708
There's a ferry over in Miya.

39:27.250 --> 39:29.416
I'm sure the others will use---

39:43.416 --> 39:44.750
Your face…

39:45.250 --> 39:46.333
Huh?

39:50.916 --> 39:53.166
I guess I was mistaken.

39:53.916 --> 39:56.125
What on earth is this nonsense?

40:46.000 --> 40:49.083
Not him either, wouldn't you know…

41:20.541 --> 41:22.125
Gentosai…

41:27.416 --> 41:28.833
Have you found anything?

41:28.916 --> 41:29.833
Yes.

41:37.750 --> 41:38.666
Come in.

41:41.000 --> 41:43.000
We've identified the source of the guns.

41:43.083 --> 41:44.291
Go on.

41:44.375 --> 41:45.583
We've examined the records

41:45.666 --> 41:47.833
of every smuggler
taken into custody recently,

41:48.500 --> 41:50.666
and we found information
about a large shipment

41:50.750 --> 41:52.875
brought into Yokohama from Britain.

41:56.666 --> 41:58.333
To our surprise,

41:58.916 --> 42:01.833
the shipment contained
over 100 Snider rifles.

42:01.916 --> 42:02.875
Impossible.

42:02.958 --> 42:07.041
How could a smuggler have enough money
to bring in hundreds of Snider rifles?

42:07.833 --> 42:10.750
Exactly.
He was acting on someone's behalf.

42:11.750 --> 42:13.041
On whose?

42:18.416 --> 42:19.416
Mitsui.

42:21.708 --> 42:22.625
Sumitomo.

42:25.125 --> 42:26.166
Yasuda.

42:28.166 --> 42:29.166
Mitsubishi.

42:30.625 --> 42:32.833
Those four paid for the shipment.

42:35.416 --> 42:37.666
They are the four zaibatsu

42:39.208 --> 42:40.916
who support the Meiji government.

43:05.750 --> 43:08.458
95 REMAINING
